    "description": "Storehouse, level 2 of 3: L1 plus flourish 2. Needs scaffolding: 13 tall (over the 9 rule; the roof is within reach from the hall floor at y 3, so the planner may need little or none). Over budget on purpose (Carlton: bigger, more storage). Jettied timber hall (plaster in a dark oak frame, spruce roof) on a stone undercroft cellar; outside stone stair to the door, inside stair to the cellar, back cart door. L1 some chests and barrels; L2 barrel racks, chests two high, hoist, loading awning; L3 loft full of chests, cellar full, yard, flowers. Not yet builder-tested: lectern. Decoration step adds: item.",
    "changes": "Carlton: \"needs to be larger, add a cellar, more chests, should scale with levels\". Much bigger (hall 9 by 13 instead of 8 by 9) and on two floors plus a loft. The cellar: the mod cannot build below the ground (no layers under 0, builders never dig), so it is a raised stone undercroft: the hall stands on it one storey up (reached by an outside stone stair), and a railed stair inside goes down to it; carts also get in through a back door at ground level. No ladders. Storage grows per level: L1 12 chests and 16 barrels; L2 28 chests and 61 barrels (racks of barrels on their sides, everything two high, the cellar lined); L3 adds the loft under the roof full of chests (its own stair), fills the cellar and adds a goods lean-to and a wood yard outside: 76 chests and 71 barrels. 13 tall: marked as needing scaffolding.",
    "parent": 1,
    "reviewedAt": null,
